# QUESTION : LOAD BALANCER KYA HOTA HAI ?
===========================================

Load Balancer ek intermediate component hota hai jo incoming client requests ko multiple backend servers 
jaha par different service instances deployed hoti hain — ke beech distribute karta hai. 

Iska primary purpose hai:

- Traffic ko evenly distribute karna jisse kisi ek server par overload prevent ho
- Kisi ek server ke fail hone par baaki healthy servers ko traffic dena (High Availability)



------------------------------------------------------------------
## QUESTION : LOAD BALANCER KE TYPES — DEPLOYMENT KE BASIS PAR ?
------------------------------------------------------------------

Load Balancers ko mainly do tarah se classify kiya jaata hai:

1: Hardware Load Balancers (Traditional)
------------------------------------------

Traditionally, Load Balancers dedicated hardware appliances hote the.

Inke andar specialized hardware (optimized processors, high-speed networking hardware, etc.)
ke saath vendor-provided Load Balancing software pre-installed hota tha.

Examples:

    - F5 BIG-IP
    - Citrix NetScaler
    - A10 Thunder


### BENEFITS:
---------------
- Very high performance (dedicated hardware)
- Reliable aur stable
- Vendor support available


### LIMITATIONS:
------------------
- Expensive 
- Scaling ke liye naya hardware kharidna padta hai
- Cloud environments ke saath integrate karna difficult



2. Software Load Balancers (Modern)
-------------------------------------

Aaj ke modern cloud environments me dedicated hardware Load Balancers ki jagah
zyadatar software-based Load Balancers use kiye jaate hain.

Ye software (jaise NGINX, HAProxy, Envoy, Traefik, etc.) Virtual Machines (VMs) ya Containers
par run karte hain aur incoming client requests ko multiple backend servers jaha par different
service instances deployed hote hain unke beech distribute karte hai. 

Cloud providers managed Load Balancer bhi dete hain:

- AWS Elastic Load Balancer (ELB)
- Azure Load Balancer
- Google Cloud Load Balancer


### BENEFITS:
---------------

- Hardware-based LBs se sasta hota hai (hardware kharidne ki zaroorat nahi, VM/Container par run karta hai)
- Horizontal scaling easy (traffic badhe to bas naya instance spin up kar do)

### LIMITATIONS :
------------------

- Hardware Load Balancer ke comparison me performance thodi kam
- OS / VM level par tuning karni padti hai




